<article class="env-lemma" id="00R5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00R5">Lemma <span data-tag="00R5">10.112.9</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. Assume $R$ Cohen-Macaulay. If $S$ is finite flat over $R$, or if $S$ is flat over $R$ and $\dim (S) \leq \dim (R)$, then $S$ is Cohen-Macaulay and $\dim (R) = \dim (S)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x_1, \ldots , x_ d \in \mathfrak m_ R$ be a regular sequence of length $d = \dim (R)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00LM" data-tag="00LM">10.68.5</a> this maps to a regular sequence in $S$. Hence $S$ is Cohen-Macaulay if $\dim (S) \leq d$. This is true if $S$ is finite flat over $R$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/00OK" data-tag="00OK">10.112.4</a>. And in the second case we assumed it. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>